+### Stage-6 validated graph banks and activation permits
+
+A planner cannot safely publish a domain change and then attempt an ordinary
+fallible graph commit. The generic extension instead separates owning admission
+from activation authority. Opt-in fixed slots retain fully validated graph owners
+at a recorded runtime epoch; scope/generation IDs identify each admitted attempt.
+The existing callback-wide validator allowance applies, and rejected or released
+owners return through existing command completion credits.
+
+`GraphAccess` in operation/planning contexts lends an exclusive `GraphActivation`
+permit only after readiness, epoch/exhaustion, storage and pending MIDI checks.
+The planner performs all fallible domain work first. It may then publish its
+preflighted state and consume the permit for an infallible metadata/epoch swap,
+retaining the displaced owner. Dropping the permit changes nothing; it does not
+undo domain mutations. Views cannot cross activation or escape the callback, and
+outside code cannot construct authority. No loop concepts enter the generic API.
+
+A planning-time change cannot remove a node with already-delivered MIDI waiting
+in its injection buffer: explicit Busy refusal preserves that frame's execution
+instead of dropping the packet or replaying it when the node later returns.
+Operation-time activation precedes MIDI delivery under existing scheduler order;
+a subsequently missing target receives InvalidId. Recovery operation contexts
+cannot activate. This does not provide domain-specific note or role cleanup.
+
+Plan accounting includes vector capacity, not just populated rows. Checked stage
+budgets conservatively cover all retained candidates plus one compatible active
+owner. Staging never enlarges descriptor storage; compiler temporaries and command
+owners remain separate preparation costs. The ownership swap is constant work;
+preflight's prepared node/input-port scan is finite, not a deadline guarantee.
+
+See `src/rust/rt_runtime/docs/graph-activation.md` and
+`docs/loop_layer/evidence/graph-activation-stage6{,-provenance}.json`. Guarded
+native/Wasm scenarios, generation/epoch limits, lifetime refusals and legacy
+NoPlanner/worklet regressions pass. New Miri coverage is queued for consolidated
+Stage6 verification. General loop graph/role-generation/media transactions and
+the independent loop hosts remain incomplete.
